# core.autocrlf would otherwise check these out with CRLF endings, which breaks them:
#
#   .htaccess  - Apache treats a trailing \r as part of a directive's value, and a
#                line-continuation backslash followed by \r\n stops continuing the line.
#   *.sh       - a shell script with CRLF fails to run on Linux ("bad interpreter: ^M").
#
# The site is a static export, so public/.htaccess is copied verbatim into out/ and
# uploaded to the server exactly as it appears in the working tree.
.htaccess text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
